  "details": "I know IK to World interaction was mentioned in another post\n\n(https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/make-the-avatar-ik-able-to-react-to-objects-in-the-world)\n\nbut since it's been a while I'd like to suggest a (theoretically) easier approach - allow creators to manually override an avatar's target transforms, even if it's just hands. This kind of thing would open up possibilities for tons of unique, interactive features including not only the obvious world collisions but buttons, door handles, weighted objects, even avatar interactions like dynamic high fives or hugs could be arranged.\n\nWithout much knowledge of VRC internals, it's my best guess that this would behave almost as an extension of the Stations code, which already provides some access to an avatar's animator. It might also be easier on creators to just have a built-in \"IK Transform Override\" object of some sort in Udon, assuming it's not too much work on y'alls end.",
